This extension adds Uncharted: Legacy of Thieves Collection modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]You need to enable mods in Fluffy for them to be loaded by the game.[/summary]

This extension is intended to be used in combination with[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/site/mods/818] Fluffy Mod Manager[/url] (FMM). That mod will install automatically after installing this extension.
[color=#ffe599][b][size=4]You need to enable mods in Fluffy Mod Manger for them to be installed to the game files! There is a tool included with the extension, so you will see a button for Fluffy in the Dashboard tab or at the top of the Vortex window.[/size][/b][/color]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]GOG[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Fluffy Mod Manager installs to the game folder, recognised by a "modmanager.exe" file.[/*]
[*]PSARC Files mods with a ".psarc" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Any other mod not described above installs to the "Games\UC4\Mods" folder.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]For mods not to be used with Fluffy Mod Manager (upscalers, reshades, etc.), you will need to change the mod type to "Binaries / Root Game Folder" and unzip the mod files in the staging folder. This is necessary because the default Fluffy Mod Manger mods need to be kept in their zips for easier management with Fluffy.[/*]
[*]Mods with .psarc files can't be installed with Fluffy, and will be automatically installed into the "Uncharted4_data" folder.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Uncharted: Legacy of Thieves Collection mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Fluffy Mod Manager (tool):

This installer handles Fluffy Mod Manager, not mods for it. It exists so users can install Fluffy Mod Manager through Vortex, and mod authors normally never package this.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a file named "modmanager.exe" in the archive.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - If you bundle Fluffy Mod Manager inside your mod archive, Vortex treats the whole download as Fluffy Mod Manager rather than as your mod. Ship the mod alone and list Fluffy Mod Manager as a requirement.

========================================================================

PSARC Files:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".psarc" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Fluffy-Format Mods:

The catch-all for RE Engine mods packaged in the normal Fluffy Mod Manager layout. Most content mods for this game land here, which is the intended outcome.

  Requirements:
    - Any archive not claimed by an earlier installer is treated as a Fluffy-format mod.
    - An archive already zipped in the Fluffy layout is installed as it is, with no repacking.

  Installs to: "Games\UC4\Mods"

  Common mistakes:
    - Because this is a catch-all, a badly laid-out archive still installs - it just may not work. Match the layout Fluffy Mod Manager expects.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]
